execution/v2.4/receipts/W05/W05-99/qualification_failure_revision02_architecture_codex/20261015-current-chat\C-ARCHITECTURE.md:22:Do not call recoverArtifact: its author and use records belong to the old executor. Do not call serverArtifactMode: it emits OBSERVED. Do not append the new MANIFEST to old result_artifact_ids or the native output list. `run_id=null` means runtime_uploads, artifact_uses and artifact_use_proofs each have **zero** new rows. One DERIVED_FROM ImpactLink ties the new proof to profile. Contract fixtures must pass the actual immutable schema24 Artifact/ImpactLink/VersionRef schemas before Source acceptance.
execution/v2.4/receipts/W05/W05-99/qualification_failure_revision02_architecture_codex/20261015-current-chat\C-ARCHITECTURE.md:32:The schema24 transaction uses one existing DB connection and one transaction with a proven SQLite write reservation. Revalidate full schema and before census, all CAS subjects, current Owner/Host/root and immutable evidence. No constructor that calls store.Open migrations, Service.New/NewCurrentMu, Host.New bootstrap, provider/vault/coordinator or listeners is allowed. New store helper opens existing `mode=rw`, refuses absent DB/URI aliases, validates WAL/FULL/foreign-key settings on this maintenance connection and exact schema fingerprint (sqlite_master tables, indexes, triggers/views + migration rows + contracts hashes), and takes the reservation before CAS. Source must prove its transaction primitive is compatible with the tx-aware domain writers; no nested BEGIN/implicit helper transaction.
